-- title:
--   Regular stalks of X_O away from the crossing points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a `DRModelPackage` for $p$, that is, a bundle of data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field at level $p$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ (properness, flatness and integrality of `DRModel.toBase p`, integral closedness of the sections over affine opens, curve models of the fibres over $\mathbb{Q}$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with their compatibilities, two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$ over $\mathbb{Z}$, a distinguished open `smoothLocus` that is smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ and contains every open smooth over $\mathbb{Z}$, and further data including the morphisms `compInf` and `compZero` attached to a field). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $z$ be a point of the fibre product $\mathfrak{X}_O$ of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ such that: $z$ does not lie in the preimage under the second projection of the basic open $D(p) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} O$, so $z$ lies over the closed point; and $z$ is not the image of any point $n$ of the fibre product of $\mathfrak{X}$`.compInf κ` with $\mathfrak{X}$`.compZero κ` under the composite of the first projection, then $\mathfrak{X}$`.compInf κ`, then `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` (the map $\mathfrak{X}_\kappa \to \mathfrak{X}_O$ induced by the identity on `DRModel p` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{to}\kappa$). Then the stalk of the structure sheaf of $\mathfrak{X}_O$ at $z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the regularity statement for the Deligne–Rapoport model after base change to a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$: every point of the special fibre other than the finitely many points where the two components of the geometric special fibre cross has a regular local ring. It is used in the construction of a resolved model package for $p$ (`exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`), where the crossing points are the only places needing attention.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_forall_ne_baseChangeMap_crossing.lean

